# Build output. The repo-root .gitignore has no Rust entries, so without
# this a `git add packages/sdk-rust` stages several hundred megabytes of
# compiled rustls/ring artifacts.
/target

# Cargo.lock IS committed. Cargo's default advice is that a library omits it,
# but this crate's whole dependency argument is "three crates, and here is
# the tree you inherit" — pinning it means a reviewer can see that tree, and
# a cold build resolves to what the test output in the changelog describes.
